    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268">

                <pb facs="1042" n="892" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg892"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2151/33–35.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the French
                        Chargé.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-08-13"><hi rendition="#italic">August 13,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 429.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 7th instant, transmitting, by instruction from his
                    excellency the <pb facs="1043" n="893" xml:id="pg893"/> minister of foreign
                    affairs, a note acquainting this Government with the measures that have been
                    adopted and were deemed indispensable to insure the restoration of order and
                    safety in Morocco in consequence of the unforeseen outbreak at Casablanca.</p>
                <p>The note verbale, also transmitted by you with the above, is intended to bring
                    the particulars of these events to the department’s knowledge.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
